From 069a7d90a612d08c1621bf5434ab28615c365d07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: core agent <core@perf>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:15:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] BananaDS: core.fast_div, the divider and square root unit
 reschedule their event in one step (melonDS patch 0040; off by default:
 -0.4%)

StartDiv and StartSqrt cancelled and rescheduled their event at every parameter write (five per 64-bit divide;
~1000 divides a frame on cpubench), and each cancel of the earliest event set the scheduler's SchedNext to 0, a
walk of the event list at the next slice. NDS::RescheduleEvent does both in one step with the same event, mask,
CPU target and SchedNext as the pair, and keeps SchedNext known when the event stays the earliest. Exact
(pictures, audio, main RAM every frame). rgds-sim, cpubench-thumb: -0.4% of the main thread, so it stays off
(core.fast_div=on turns it on; SetFastDiv).
---
 bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md                     |   1 +
 ...and-square-root-unit-reschedule-thei.patch | 129 ++++++++++++++++++
 bananads/src/emu.cpp                          |   4 +
 3 files changed, 134 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 bananads/patches/melonds/0040-NDS-the-divider-and-square-root-unit-reschedule-thei.patch

